    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "DSA_SIGNALS",
      "narration": "Three phrasings cover most of it. Number of ways, which is counting rather than listing. Minimum or maximum cost, where you're optimising. Longest or shortest something. And the real test: can the answer for n be built from answers to smaller versions of n? If the question wants the actual list rather than a count, that's backtracking from the previous pattern. And if a locally best choice is always globally right, greedy is cheaper. Counting, optimising, and built from smaller answers. Those three together mean dynamic programming.",
      "durationFrames": 997,
      "timingSource": "tts",
      "background": "zoneA",
