    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "DSA_TRACE_DP",
      "narration": "You're climbing a staircase of five steps, and each move is either one step or two. How many different ways are there to reach the top? Your first instinct is to try every possibility, and for five stairs that's fine: stair one, stair two, stair three, stair four, stair five, and the answer comes out at eight. But try that on forty stairs and your laptop will still be thinking about it tomorrow, because the work doubles with every stair.",
      "durationFrames": 750,
      "timingSource": "tts",
      "background": "zoneC",
